<title>USA: N. Carolina jobless rate hits seven-year low.</title>
<headline>N. Carolina jobless rate hits seven-year low.</headline>
<dateline>RALEIGH, N.C. 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>North Carolina's unemployment rate dipped to 3.8 percent in January from 4.2 percent in December, the state Employment Security Commission said Friday.</p>
<p>The January rate was down from 4.8 percent a year ago and was the state's lowest rate since April 1990, when the unemployment rate fell to 3.7 percent.</p>
<p>The state added more than 24,000 jobs during the month, the commission said.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
